text:
This is not a joke post, this is an attempt at an analysis.

&amp;#x200B;

Morbius

Morbius was hated by fans and became the largest meme of 2022 just because of how bad it was. "Its morbin time" was extremely common. The marketing was horrible and casuals had no clue if it was a new MCU film or if spiderman had anything to do with it.  


Box Office

Morbius though hated, had a great opening weekend of almost 40 million domestically, but it then cratered dropping a record  -73.8% percent, after finishing its run Morbius was such a big meme that Sony did a disastrous re-relase. 

75\*2.5= 187.5 break even point.

&amp;#x200B;

The movie made  **$167,460,961.** 

Only 20 million below its break-even point. After VOD sales and the Netflix contract it is very likely the movie actually turned a profit.

&amp;#x200B;

Conclusion

Sony is a studio that greenlit a movie about an insanely unknown character that appeared rarely in spiderman. It is very possible they might greenlight a sequel hoping that everyone laughs at it and its a meme and people go and see it like Gentleminions and Barbenheimer. 

Sony is desperate for money and they might in that pursuit greenlight Morbius 2. I would guess they would probably name it "Morbius: It's Morbin Time"

&amp;#x200B;

TLDR: Sony probably made profit from Morbius and is dumb enough to greenlight a sequel.

&amp;#x200B;

What are your thoughts...

&amp;#x200B;

